2 Enterprise, business growth and size	8	What is an 'entrepreneur'?	A person who has an idea for a new business, starts it up, and accepts the risks of the new business venture.	Definition
2 Enterprise, business growth and size	9	List four key characteristics of a successful entrepreneur.	Hard-working, risk taker, optimistic, self-confident, innovative, independent, effective communicator.	4-Mark
2 Enterprise, business growth and size	10	What is a 'business plan' and why is it important?	A written document describing a business, its objectives, strategies, market, and financial forecasts. It forces the entrepreneur to think ahead, provides guidelines, and helps convince banks/investors to provide finance.	4-Mark
2 Enterprise, business growth and size	11	State three main elements included in a business plan.	Any three from: Business objectives, Market research, Marketing strategy, Human resources plan, Operations details, Financial forecasts.	Core Question
2 Enterprise, business growth and size	12	Why do governments support business start-ups?	To reduce unemployment, increase competition/consumer choice, increase total economic output, benefit society, and encourage future large businesses.	4-Mark
2 Enterprise, business growth and size	13	Identify four methods used to measure the size of a business.	Number of employees, 2) Value of output/sales, 3) Volume of output/sales, 4) Value of capital employed.	4-Mark
2 Enterprise, business growth and size	14	Explain why 'number of employees' might give a misleading measure of business size.	A capital-intensive firm with high automation might employ very few workers but produce huge output/sales value compared to a labor-intensive firm.	2-Mark
