16 Marketing strategy, entering new markets in other countries and legal controls	92	State two benefits and two challenges of entering international markets.	Benefits: Increased total sales volume; spreads business risks across countries. Challenges: Cultural differences/language barriers; lack of local knowledge; import tariffs and legal differences.	4-Mark
16 Marketing strategy, entering new markets in other countries and legal controls	93	Give three examples of consumer protection laws impacting marketing.	Weights and measures laws, 2) Misleading promotion controls, 3) Product quality/fitness for purpose rules, 4) Misleading price reduction controls.	4-Mark
