17 Production of goods and services	95	Distinguish between 'labour-intensive' and 'capital-intensive' production.	Labour-intensive: Uses a large proportion of manual labour relative to machinery. Capital-intensive: Uses a high proportion of machinery/automation relative to workers.	4-Mark
