18 Technology and production of goods and services	102	What do CAD and CAM stand for?	CAD: Computer-Aided Design. CAM: Computer-Aided Manufacturing.	2-Mark
18 Technology and production of goods and services	103	Define 'EPOS' and explain its primary advantage.	Electronic Point of Sale. It scans barcodes at tills to display prices and automatically updates inventory records for automatic reordering.	2-Mark
19 Sustainable production of goods and services	104	Define 'sustainable production' and 'renewable energy'.	Sustainable production: Minimising the use of natural resources, hazardous materials, and pollution to preserve resources for the future. Renewable energy: Power obtained from infinite sources that do not get depleted (e.g., solar, wind).	4-Mark
19 Sustainable production of goods and services	105	Differentiate between 'reusing' and 'recycling'.	Reusing: Using an item again without alteration (e.g., refilling glass bottles). Recycling: Processing waste materials to convert them into new products.	4-Mark
20 Costs, scale of production and break-even analysis	106	Define 'fixed costs' and 'variable costs' and give one example of each.	Fixed costs: Costs that do not vary with output level in the short run (e.g., rent, manager salaries). Variable costs: Costs that vary directly with output level (e.g., raw materials, piece-rate wages).	4-Mark
